.\" Educational secure-coding reference. Generated, not hand-edited.
.TH CWE-787 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-787 \- Out\-of\-bounds Write
.SH RANK
2025 CWE Top 25 rank: \fB#5\fR (2024 rank: 2).
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: Memory Safety.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Data is written past the end (or before the start) of an intended buffer, corrupting adjacent memory: other variables, heap metadata, return addresses or function pointers. Leads to crashes, data corruption or code execution. Managed runtimes (Java, Go, Python, Node) bounds\-check and largely prevent this class; the examples are therefore in C and C++.
.SH MITIGATION
Bound every write by the destination size (snprintf, memcpy with a validated length). In C++ prefer std::string / std::vector. Enable FORTIFY_SOURCE, stack canaries and AddressSanitizer; consider Rust for new components.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB106\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
